      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "path": "/notes",
    "before": "Source specifies0.1M Tris/HCl,pH7.5; nominal total Tris moiety concentration retained, not independent concentrations for acid and conjugate base. Solvent and neutralization ratio unreported. Raw assigned source label: 0.1 M Tris/HCl (pH7.5). Quantities in notes preserve source preparation and are not final-medium concentrations. No global synonym is added for this context-dependent label.",
    "after": "Source specifies0.1M Tris/HCl,pH7.5; nominal total Tris moiety concentration retained, not independent concentrations for acid and conjugate base. Solvent and neutralization ratio unreported. Raw assigned source label: 0.1 M Tris/HCl (pH7.5). Quantities in notes preserve source preparation and are not final-medium concentrations. No global synonym is added for this context-dependent label. Issue1237 W01-PREP-B-001: NBRC1507 names 0.1 M Tris/HCl (pH7.5) as a supplied buffer. It does not enumerate free hydrochloric acid as a separately added component. Retain the named buffer moiety and nominal strength; the complete constituent list, solvent, preparation and neutralization ratio remain unknown. No dry Tris-HCl substitution or neutralization chemistry is inferred."
  }
]
B-PROPOSAL-jcm_1479_l_cysteine_hcl_monohydrate_5_percent_ph7 [
  {
    "path": "/notes",
    "before": "Nominal source-qualified stock only. pH7.0 and1mladdition explicit; percentagebasis,solvent,pHadjustment reagent unreported. The source does not establish a complete constituent list; no omitted solvent or titrant is invented. Raw source labels retained in linked frozen cases: ['5% L-Cysteine·HCl·H2O solution (pH 7.0)']. Generic labels are not global resolving synonyms. No pre-existing WITHHOLD or REJECTED gate is lifted.",
    "after": "Nominal source-qualified stock only. pH7.0 and1mladdition explicit; percentagebasis,solvent,pHadjustment reagent unreported. The source does not establish a complete constituent list; no omitted solvent or titrant is invented. Raw source labels retained in linked frozen cases: ['5% L-Cysteine·HCl·H2O solution (pH 7.0)']. Generic labels are not global resolving synonyms. No pre-existing WITHHOLD or REJECTED gate is lifted. Issue1237 W01-PREP-B-002/CHEM-COMP-003: JCM1479 explicitly specifies the L-cysteine hydrochloride monohydrate 5% stock at pH7.0. It is a preparation, separate from solid solute. Unreported pH in another 5% stock establishes neither difference nor equivalence. Percentage basis, carrier and titrant/preparation remain unreported; a common-stock relationship requires affirmative source evidence."
  }
]
W07-COMBINED-JCM900-JCM979-Hutner [
  {
    "path": "/notes",
    "before": "The primary JCM 900 and JCM 979 stock subrecipes specify the same nine named inputs, quantities, Metals 44 reference to JCM 149 and preparation: dissolve NTA, adjust to pH 7.0 with about 7.3 g KOH, add the remaining ingredients, and readjust to pH 6.8 with NaOH or H2SO4. Parent media and vitamin supplements differ outside this stock boundary. The literal malformed (NH4)6MoO24·4H2O remains unresolved; no heptamolybdate correction or exact chemical-component equivalence is asserted. Raw source names Hutner's basal salts (see below) and Modified Hutner's basal salts remain in the frozen case evidence; neither becomes a global stock synonym. The canonical proposed local registry identifier retains JCM 900 provenance and also covers this verified JCM 979 subrecipe.",
    "after": "The primary JCM 900 and JCM 979 stock subrecipes specify the same nine named inputs, quantities, Metals 44 reference to JCM 149 and preparation: dissolve NTA, adjust to pH 7.0 with about 7.3 g KOH, add the remaining ingredients, and readjust to pH 6.8 with NaOH or H2SO4. Parent media and vitamin supplements differ outside this stock boundary. The literal malformed (NH4)6MoO24·4H2O remains unresolved; no heptamolybdate correction or exact chemical-component equivalence is asserted. Raw source names Hutner's basal salts (see below) and Modified Hutner's basal salts remain in the frozen case evidence; neither becomes a global stock synonym. The canonical proposed local registry identifier retains JCM 900 provenance and also covers this verified JCM 979 subrecipe. Issue1237 MIN-F02: Comparison with DSM590/1144 remains unresolved at complete chemical/preparation scope. JCM149 Metals44 prints EDTA·2Na and MnSO4·xH2O; DSM prints Na-EDTA and MnSO4·H2O plus a few drops of concentrated H2SO4. Unspecified hydration, salt detail or an unreported acid step does not prove incompatibility or equivalence. The historical malformed molybdate strings remain literal unresolved assertions. Positively different JCM149 outer Hutner mineral base has MgSO4·7H2O 14.45 g versus 29.7 g in JCM900/979; that outer recipe is distinct from the nested Metals44 reference. JCM631 also retains its positively different Mg/Ca quantities and vitamin inputs. All present immediate inputs remain unchanged; COMPLETE is source-list completeness, not resolved molecular identity."
  }
]
